        "name": "Eye Rays",
        "description": "The beholder randomly shoots one of the following magical rays at a target it can see within 120 feet of itself (roll 1d10; reroll if the beholder has already used that ray during this turn): 1: Charm Ray: Wisdom saving throw DC 16. On a failed save, 13 (3d8) Psychic damage, and the target has the Charmed condition for 1 hour or until it takes damage. On a success, Half damage only. 2: Paralyzing Ray: Constitution saving throw DC 16. On a failed save, The target has the Paralyzed condition and repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically. 3: Fear Ray: Wisdom saving throw DC 16. On a failed save, 14 (4d6) Psychic damage, and the target has the Frightened condition until the end of its next turn. On a success, Half damage only. 4: Slowing Ray: Constitution saving throw DC 16. On a failed save, 18 (4d8) Necrotic damage. Until the end of the target's next turn, the target's Speed is halved; the target can't take Reactions; and it can take either an action or a Bonus Action on its turn, not both. On a success, Half damage only. 5: Enervation Ray: Constitution saving throw DC 16. On a failed save, 13 (3d8) Poison damage, and the target has the Poisoned condition until the end of its next turn. While Poisoned, the target can't regain Hit Points. On a success, Half damage only. 6: Telekinetic Ray: Strength saving throw DC 16 (the target succeeds automatically if it is Gargantuan). On a failed save, The beholder moves the target up to 30 feet in any direction. The target has the Restrained condition until the start of the beholder's next turn or until the beholder has the Incapacitated condition. The beholder can also exert fine control on objects with this ray, such as manipulating a tool or opening a door or container. 7: Sleep Ray: Wisdom saving throw DC 16 (the target succeeds automatically if it is a Construct or an Undead). On a failed save, The target has the Unconscious condition for 1 minute. The condition ends if the target takes damage or a creature within 5 feet of it takes an action to wake it. 8: Petrification Ray: Constitution saving throw DC 16. 1 The target has the Restrained condition and repeats the save at the end of its next turn if it is still Restrained, ending the effect on itself on a success. 2 The target has the Petrified condition instead of the Restrained condition. 9: Disintegration Ray: Dexterity saving throw DC 16. On a failed save, 36 (8d8) Force damage. If the target is a nonmagical object or a creation of magical force, a 10-foot Cube [Area of Effect] of it disintegrates into dust. On a success, Half damage. Regardless of the save, If the target is a creature and this damage reduces it to 0 Hit Points, it disintegrates into dust. 10: Death Ray: Dexterity saving throw DC 16. On a failed save, 55 (10d10) Necrotic damage. On a success, Half damage. Regardless of the save, The target dies if the ray reduces it to 0 Hit Points.",
