        "name": "Eye Rays",
        "description": "The zombie randomly shoots one of the following magical rays at a target it can see within 120 feet of itself (roll 1d4; reroll if the zombie has already used that ray during this turn): 1: Paralyzing Ray: Constitution saving throw DC 14. On a failed save, The target has the Paralyzed condition and repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically. 2: Fear Ray: Wisdom saving throw DC 14. On a failed save, 13 (3d8) Psychic damage, and the target has the Frightened condition until the end of its next turn. 3: Enervation Ray: Constitution saving throw DC 14. On a failed save, 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage, and the target has the Poisoned condition until the end of its next turn. While Poisoned, the target can't regain Hit Points. On a success, Half damage only. 4: Disintegration Ray: Dexterity saving throw DC 14. On a failed save, 27 (5d10) Force damage. If the target is a nonmagical object or a creation of magical force, a 10-foot Cube [Area of Effect] of it disintegrates into dust. On a success, Half damage. Regardless of the save, If the target is a creature and this damage reduces it to 0 Hit Points, it disintegrates into dust.",
