        "id": "cataclysmic_event",
        "name": "Cataclysmic Event",
        "description": "The cataclysm creates one of the following effects at random (roll 1d4): 1: Clinging Flames: Dexterity saving throw DC 23, each creature in a 60-foot-radius Sphere [Area of Effect] centered on a point the cataclysm can see within 150 feet. On a failed save, 45 (13d6) Fire damage. On a success, Half damage. Regardless of the save, The target starts burning. 2: Freezing Waves: Strength saving throw DC 23, each creature in a 90-foot Cone [Area of Effect]. On a failed save, 22 (5d8) Bludgeoning damage plus 22 (5d8) Cold damage, and the target has the Prone condition. On a success, Half damage only. Regardless of the save, The target's Speed is reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn. 3: Raging Storm: A storm cloud fills a 60-foot-radius Sphere [Area of Effect] centered on a point the cataclysm can see within 150 feet. The cloud lasts for 1 minute or until the cataclysm uses Cataclysmic Event again. Creatures entirely in the cloud have the Blinded and Deafened conditions and can't cast spells with a Verbal component. Dexterity saving throw DC 23, each creature that enters the cloud for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there. On a failed save, 18 (4d8) Lightning damage plus 18 (4d8) Thunder damage. On a success, Half damage. 4: Swallowing Earth: Strength saving throw DC 23, each creature in a 90-foot Cube [Area of Effect] originating from a point on the ground within 150 feet. On a failed save, 18 (4d8) Bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) Acid damage, and the target has the Prone condition and is buried under rubble. A buried target has the Restrained condition, has Cover, and is suffocating. As an action, a buried creature or another creature within 5 feet of it can make a DC 18 Strength (Athletics) check. On a successful check, the creature is no longer buried. On a success, Half damage only.",
